they should be, and that leads to this dislike when they go over the line, when they tread where they're not supposed to be. There are other aspects to the double-bind. Female leaders can get in trouble for displaying emotion, but also for not displaying emotion. Lisa Feldman Barrett is a psychology professor at Northeastern University and author of the book How Emotions Are Made. There is an implication that if a woman expresses emotion that she's either unsuitable for leadership are made. In one experiment, Lisa showed volunteers pictures of faces
行事有着非常强烈的看法，当他们越界时，当他们涉足不该涉足的领域时，就会引发这种厌恶。双重约束还有其他方面。女性领导者不仅因为表现出情绪而陷入麻烦，也因为没有表现出情绪而陷入麻烦。莉萨·费尔德曼·巴雷特 (Lisa Feldman Barrett) 是东北大学的心理学教授，也是《情绪是如何产生的》(How Emotions Are Made) 一书的作者。这里有一种暗示，如果女性表达情绪，说明她要么不适合领导地位或制造麻烦。在一个实验中，莉萨向志愿者展示了面孔图片

28
00:16:46.000 --> 00:17:10.000
and asked why the subject was expressing an emotion. She found that the volunteers thought men's emotions were shaped by what was going on around them, but that women's emotions were shaped by their nature. Both men and women, when they were looking at female faces expressing emotion, believed that this was caused by a woman's emotional nature. She's just a neurotic person.
并询问为什么主体在表达情绪。她发现志愿者认为男性的情绪是由他们周围发生的事情决定的，而女性的情绪是由她们的本性决定的。无论男女，当他们看着女性面孔表达情绪时，都认为这是由女性的情绪本性引起的。她只是一个神经过敏的人。

29
00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:45.000
She's just unstable. She's just untrustworthy, as opposed to when they were looking at male faces expressing emotion, they were more likely to say, oh, he's just having a bad day, something bad happened to him. Lots of people have suggested ways out of the double bind. Some say women should ignore criticisms about incompetence and plunge full steam ahead. If they then appear unlikable, they should also go out of their way to demonstrate kindness
她只是不稳定。她只是不可信，而相比之下，当他们看着男性面孔表达情绪时，他们更有可能说，哦，他只是今天过得不好，发生了不好的事情。许多人提出了摆脱双重约束的方法。有些人说女性应该忽视对能力不足的批评，全力以赴地向前推进。如果她们随后显得不讨人喜欢，她们也应该竭尽全力表现出善良

30
00:17:45.000 --> 00:18:18.000
in order to keep people from seeing them as competent but cold. There is something disturbing about these ideas. They ask women who are the victims here to compensate for the biases of others. Many experts also think that a society changes, our stereotypes will change as well. If more women make it through the labyrinth and get to the top, fewer people will have trouble seeing women as leaders. Many countries and organizations are coming to think of leadership as being collaborative rather than dictatorial.
以防止人们认为她们有能力但冷酷。这些想法中有一些令人不安的地方。它们要求作为受害者的女性去弥补他人的偏见。许多专家还认为，随着社会的发展，我们的刻板印象也会改变。如果有更多的女性穿过迷宫并登上顶峰，就会有更少的人难以将女性视为领导者。许多国家和组织开始将领导力视为协作式而非独裁式的。

31
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:59.000
